n Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's special Senate election pits appointed Republican incumbent Jon Husted against former Senator Sherrod Brown, with the state's Republican lean of about five points colliding with a midterm environment that has favored Democrats all year. Polling through mid-October shows Brown ahead by roughly three to four points on average, with high-quality pollsters clustering between three and six points and Republican-leaning firms showing a much closer race. Nonpartisan raters are split between Tossup and Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Brown's chances near two-thirds.\n\nMoney tells a mixed story: Brown has raised far more, but Husted holds a cash-on-hand edge and benefits from outside groups attacking Brown. Headlines note Republican worries about turnout and a heavy advertising war on Ohio airwaves. The forecast gives Brown a modest edge, with Husted's incumbency and Ohio's fundamentals keeping the race well within reach for Republicans.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7417, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7438, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7437, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6872, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6759, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6875, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.716, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_d